    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Jackson Merrill**, who anchors our lineup with a 75.10 efficiency score. Facing a soft matchup against Merrill Kelly (xERA 5.37), **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a favorable platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for R and RBI production. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson** follow closely behind with scores of 69.47 and 68.72, respectively. Despite a difficult matchup against D.J. Peterson, **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite park factor (+16%) and high-leverage spot in the order keep his output projections robust, even with the inherent risk of a tough lefty on the bump. **Cole Carrigg** remains a high-value play as well, capitalizing on a weak 5.99 xERA from Whisenhunt to provide balanced contributions across our 5x5 categories.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on the bench, where **Wade Meckler** narrowly missed the final cut. With a score of 36.56, **Wade Meckler** was hampered by a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult encounter with Nathan Eovaldi, keeping him safely below our 40-point efficiency floor. While **Dominic Smith** and **Josh Lowe** both carry marginal projections, they offer higher potential for power and situational production compared to the bench depth today. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** closely; his 42.26 score is tempered by a daunting matchup against Ben Miller (xERA 2.44), and if official lineups shift his position downward, he could see a further decline in daily value. We continue to hold **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Kyle Tucker** in reserve or off-day status, awaiting their return to high-volume output to bolster our weekly caps.",
